  "verbalization": "Jatamanin E is implicated in the regulation of CWR22R through a multi-step mechanism involving the glucagon receptor. The evidence suggests that Jatamanin E directly targets the glucagon receptor, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 3-Methylthiopropyl glucosinolate and 18,19-Dihydroangustine. These compounds, in turn, have a shared target of CWR22R. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CWR22R through the glucagon receptor indicates a potential role for Jatamanin E in modulating the activity of these compounds, possibly through a common downstream effect on CWR22R. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory relationship where Jatamanin E may influence the function of the glucagon receptor, which is a critical node in the signaling cascade leading to CWR22R activation. This suggests that Jatamanin E could be a modulator of the biological processes governed by the glucagon receptor, potentially through a mechanism that involves the downstream targets of the glucagon receptor.",
